<title>USA: Schering-Plough, Genome in deal.</title>
<headline>Schering-Plough, Genome in deal.</headline>
<dateline>MADISON, N.J. 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Schering-Plough Corp said it will potentially pay Genome Therapeutics Corp about $67 million, excluding royalties, under a research collaboration the companies announced Monday to use genomics to find new therapeutics for treating asthma.</p>
<p>Of the total potential payments, about $22.5 million would stem from license fees and research payments, and $44.5 million from payments based on sales of products developed from the collaboration, Schering-Plough said.</p>
<p>Genome has all rights to diagnostic products that may result from the collaboration, Schering-Plough added.</p>
</text>
